    "readme_description": "You are given a 2D array of axis-aligned rectangles. Each `rectangle[i] = [xi1, yi1, xi2, yi2]` denotes the ith rectangle where `(xi1, yi1)` are the coordinates of the bottom-left corner, and `(xi2, yi2)` are the coordinates of the top-right corner.\n\nCalculate the total area covered by all rectangles in the plane. Any area covered by two or more rectangles should only be counted once.\n\nReturn the total area. Since the answer may be too large, return it modulo `10^9 + 7`.",
